What I Learned From Nethack Today:

  Just because noone shouts at you and no hordes of guards come
  running at you, that doesn't mean they're not angry ...

Minetown was a double bones level; two of my earlier characters had
got killed by the same soldier with a /oDeath. My elven wizard
dispatched him easily, collected and sorted the loot, visited the
shops, etc.

Then I decided to risk digging the two graves[1]. I was expecting to
have the guards after me (I knew I could handle them) but nothing
happened. "Ok, so they don't like lock-picking but don't mind
grave-robbers." I thought.

Then I spent some more time sorting my loot, visiting the shops again
etc. Until I stepped close to the guard captain.  He unexpectedly
pulled his longsword and killed me in three hits. (I was burdened at
the time, and didn't pay attention -- I just intended to pass by him.)

But at least I learned something new.

/Jorgen

[1] I was hoping to find a magic lamp there which I vaguely remembered
    one of the deceased characters having. But perhaps nothing
    interesting ever ends up in the bones-level graves themselves?

